1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,876
Two agents, two worktrees, one file.

2
00:00:02,876 --> 00:00:05,832
Both pull requests pass against main.

3
00:00:05,832 --> 00:00:08,388
Merge one, and the other breaks.

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,305
This is Bullpen.

5
00:00:11,305 --> 00:00:13,670
Source control for AI agents.

6
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:15,595
One ask.

7
00:00:15,595 --> 00:00:18,870
The orchestrator splits it into three tasks,

8
00:00:18,870 --> 00:00:21,698
and three Claude Code agents walk onto

9
00:00:21,698 --> 00:00:24,005
campus, each on its own branch.

10
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:26,769
Two agents want auth.ts.

11
00:00:26,769 --> 00:00:28,833
The first takes a live lock.

12
00:00:28,833 --> 00:00:30,897
The second waits at the door

13
00:00:30,897 --> 00:00:32,593
until the file is free.

14
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:38,205
The database agent reaches for the schema.

15
00:00:38,205 --> 00:00:40,037
The referee, a Jetson on

16
00:00:40,037 --> 00:00:41,411
the desk, says no.

17
00:00:41,411 --> 00:00:43,395
The agent reads the reason

18
00:00:43,395 --> 00:00:44,998
and changes its plan.

19
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:48,074
Don't like what one agent did?

20
00:00:48,074 --> 00:00:49,595
Undo that agent alone.

21
00:00:49,595 --> 00:00:51,393
Its commits roll back, and

22
00:00:51,393 --> 00:00:53,052
the others keep working.

23
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:56,295
Happy with another?

24
00:00:56,295 --> 00:00:58,884
Open its building, read the real diff,

25
00:00:58,884 --> 00:01:01,405
and merge through an intent card that

26
00:01:01,405 --> 00:01:03,177
says what changed and why.

27
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:06,948
Now pull the Jetson's cable.

28
00:01:06,948 --> 00:01:08,758
The referee is offline, so

29
00:01:08,758 --> 00:01:10,219
every edit is denied.

30
00:01:10,219 --> 00:01:11,680
Bullpen fails closed.

31
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:17,423
Under the pixels, everything is real.

32
00:01:17,423 --> 00:01:19,780
Agents lock a file before each edit,

33
00:01:19,780 --> 00:01:22,531
and the lock expires after ninety seconds.

34
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:26,132
Point Bullpen at any repo

35
00:01:26,132 --> 00:01:28,350
and it builds your campus.

36
00:01:28,350 --> 00:01:30,652
Each edit becomes a commit,

37
00:01:30,652 --> 00:01:32,529
tagged with its agent.

38
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:34,531
It runs on your own Claude

39
00:01:34,531 --> 00:01:36,297
subscription, with no API key.

40
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:40,014
The referee runs on separate

41
00:01:40,014 --> 00:01:42,387
hardware the agents cannot reach.

42
00:01:42,387 --> 00:01:45,623
Small on-device models write the history, and

43
00:01:45,623 --> 00:01:47,853
a secret guard scans each diff.

44
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:52,065
Bullpen stops two agents from writing the same

45
00:01:52,065 --> 00:01:54,931
file at once, and records who changed what.

46
00:01:54,931 --> 00:01:56,530
Git tracks what changed.

47
00:01:56,530 --> 00:01:59,463
Bullpen controls who's allowed to change it.
